Lost your EC2 key? Don’t panic—here’s the fix! 🔐

# Original key:
# old-key.pem = deleted or unavailable

# EC2 still has old-key.pub in authorized_keys
#
# Important:
# You cannot create old-key.pem again from old-key.pub.

# New key architecture


LOCAL COMPUTER (MobaXterm)
--------------------------------
govind       = new private key
govind.pub   = new public key

        SSH connection
        ssh -i govind ...

              |
              v

EC2 INSTANCE
--------------------------------
/home/ubuntu/.ssh/authorized_keys
        contains govind.pub

# Steps

# 1. Create a new key on your local computer:
ssh-keygen -t ed25519 -f govind

# 2. Copy the new public key:
cat govind.pub

# 3. In the EC2 browser terminal:
mkdir -p ~/.ssh
nano ~/.ssh/authorized_keys

# Paste govind.pub, save, and exit.
# Save: Ctrl+O, Enter
# Exit: Ctrl+X

chmod 600 ~/.ssh/authorized_keys

# 4. Connect with the new private key:
ssh -i /home/mobaxterm/Desktop/govind ubuntu@YOUR_EC2_PUBLIC_DNS
